cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use linen in published work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: linen
abstract: >-
  An interactive sandbox for 3D spiking neural networks in the browser.
  Neurons are points in micrometre space built through a procedural node
  graph, simulated with Izhikevich 2007 dynamics and real conduction delays
  on a reference engine, a WebGPU engine and a CUDA engine that share one
  contract, with spike-timing plasticity, a validation battery against
  published numbers, and export to Brian 2, CSV and Neo.
authors:
  - family-names: Josephson
    given-names: Seth
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: https://github.com/sethgjosephson/linen
url: https://linen.build
version: 0.1.0
keywords:
  - spiking neural network
  - Izhikevich model
  - node graph
  - WebGPU
  - neuroscience
  - simulation
